# Wire `.claude/git-hooks/pre-commit` as the dotfiles repo's pre-commit
# hook. Validates staged `.claude/` changes (YAML parse, JSON parse,
# Python syntax, typography) at commit time, catching the kinds of
# bugs that silently shipped before (e.g., the `argument-hint:` flow-
# sequence trap that broke 7 skills). Writes to the bare repo's shared
# config, which all current and future worktrees inherit automatically.
run git -C "${dotfiles}" config core.hooksPath .claude/git-hooks

